Z||000009||1FST2M6||08-12-2000||11:31 PM||||MAYBE $20-$30 more.. a pearl can just be mixed in to the clear... and a "metal flake" in to the base... ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||08-12-2000||11:48 PM||||For what it's worth- most reds with metallic mixed with the base turns more pink. Burgundy metallic is a better choice if you want a red and metallic. Red with a red or blue pearl in the clear coat looks nice, but the pearl will change the original base color- the more pearl, the more the base color is changed. Too much red pearl looks pink and too much blue looks purple. Another interesting alternative is using fine metal flake (micro-sequins) in the clear over any color. This does not change the base color any, but adds a very pronounced glitter effect. ||||reg||1
